// model-seal-run.bml -- write the seal a model file is admitted by (<file>.form-seal: "qaf-seal1:<size>:<SHA-256>").
//
//   echo '{"file":"<path>"}' | ./fkwu observe/model-seal-run.bml            dry: names the file, its size and whether a seal stands; reads no byte of it
//   echo '{"file":"<path>","go":1}' | ./fkwu observe/model-seal-run.bml     hashes the whole file with the body's SHA-256 organ (a full read in 4 GiB chunks: about a minute from a warm page cache, minutes cold, for an 80 GiB file) and writes the seal;
//                                                                            a seal that stands is never overwritten, and a file that moved while it was read gets none
//
// The session and generate doors refuse a model with no seal and verify the file against it on the first open (then a note beside the model stands for a day). Not run by a band on a real model:
// the lead's go. Check the machine first: ./fkwu observe/memory-governor-run.bml </dev/null. Every definition is form-stdlib/bml/model-seal.bml's. Exit: 0 for a seal written or already standing, 1 otherwise.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/bml/model-seal.bml
section [form.bml] {
 ms-main();
}
